// modules/notifications: preferences, server reminders and every notification sent
// (erd.md → "নোটিফিকেশন ও রিমাইন্ডার"). User and patient ids are plain uuids.

enum ReminderKind {
  DOSE_BACKUP
  FOLLOW_UP
  APPOINTMENT
  REFILL
  PERIOD

  @@schema("notifications")
}

enum ReminderStatus {
  SCHEDULED
  SENT
  CANCELLED
  FAILED

  @@schema("notifications")
}

enum NotificationChannel {
  PUSH
  SMS
  IN_APP

  @@schema("notifications")
}

enum NotificationStatus {
  QUEUED
  SENT
  DELIVERED
  FAILED

  @@schema("notifications")
}

/// Missing row = defaults (see NotificationPreferencesService).
model NotificationPreference {
  /// ref auth.User
  userId             String    @id @db.Uuid
  pushEnabled        Boolean   @default(true)
  smsEnabled         Boolean   @default(true)
  /// Local dose alarms on the phone (the app reads this).
  alarmEnabled       Boolean   @default(true)
  doseBackupDelayMin Int       @default(30) @db.SmallInt
  /// Minutes before a follow-up / appointment: [1440, 120] = 24 h and 2 h.
  followUpOffsetsMin Json      @default("[1440, 120]")
  /// Asia/Dhaka. Pushes in this window arrive silently (no sound).
  quietStart         DateTime? @db.Time(0)
  quietEnd           DateTime? @db.Time(0)
  createdAt          DateTime  @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt          DateTime  @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@schema("notifications")
}

/// A server-side reminder with its BullMQ delayed job (jobId = reminder id).
/// One SCHEDULED reminder per (kind, refId): partial unique index in the migration.
model ScheduledReminder {
  id        String                @id @default(uuid(7)) @db.Uuid
  /// ref auth.User: main recipient (handlers may add family members with receivesAlerts).
  userId    String                @db.Uuid
  /// ref users.PatientProfile
  patientId String?               @db.Uuid
  kind      ReminderKind
  /// doseLog, appointment or plan id.
  refId     String                @db.Uuid
  fireAt    DateTime              @db.Timestamptz(3)
  channels  NotificationChannel[]
  status    ReminderStatus        @default(SCHEDULED)
  jobId     String?
  sentAt    DateTime?             @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdAt DateTime              @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt DateTime              @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)

  notifications Notification[]

  @@index([kind, refId])
  @@index([patientId, status])
  @@schema("notifications")
}

/// Every delivery: one row per channel per recipient. The in-app inbox shows IN_APP rows.
model Notification {
  id            String              @id @default(uuid(7)) @db.Uuid
  /// ref auth.User
  userId        String              @db.Uuid
  /// ref users.PatientProfile: whose care this is about (for the family member's inbox).
  patientId     String?             @db.Uuid
  reminderId    String?             @db.Uuid
  channel       NotificationChannel
  /// "dose.missed", "medicine.refill"
  type          String
  title         String
  body          String
  /// Deep link for the app, e.g. { "screen": "medicine", "profileId": "…" }.
  data          Json?
  status        NotificationStatus  @default(QUEUED)
  /// Why a delivery failed (provider error code, "NO_PUSH_TOKEN"); never message content.
  failureReason String?
  providerMsgId String?
  sentAt        DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  readAt        DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdAt     DateTime            @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt     DateTime            @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)

  reminder ScheduledReminder? @relation(fields: [reminderId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  @@index([userId, readAt])
  @@index([userId, channel, createdAt])
  @@schema("notifications")
}
